course: dictionary
lesson: 4084
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Ghost is a word with more than one meaning. Most of the time it means the spirit of a dead person that some people believe can be seen or heard, as in a spooky story. Context tells you which meaning is right.
explain: Look at the words around it. Ghost stories and Halloween games point to the spooky meaning. But in «she ghosted me», ghost is a verb, and it means she stopped answering your messages and ignored you. Nobody is a spirit there.
explain: A ghost can also be a very faint trace of something, like «a ghost of a smile». That means only the tiniest bit of a smile. Ask yourself: which meaning fits this sentence? Then try it in the sentence to check.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: Ghost (noun) means the spirit of a dead person that people believe can be seen or heard, as in a ghost story.
fact: Ghost (verb, slang) means to suddenly stop answering someone's messages and ignore them.
fact: «A ghost of a smile» means a very faint trace of a smile.
fact: «Give up the ghost» is informal: for a person it means to die, and for a machine it means to stop working.
fact: «Dǎnxiǎoguǐ» is Chinese for scaredy-cat. It literally means small-gall ghost.
exercise: «The ghost of a smile crossed her face before she answered.» What does ghost of a smile mean? | *A very faint trace of a smile | A spooky picture on the wall | A big, loud laugh | A smile painted on a mask
exercise: Zara says, «He ghosted me after the party.» What does ghosted mean? | *He stopped answering her messages and ignored her | He sent her ten messages in a row | He gave her a present | He danced with her all night
exercise: «My old tablet gave up the ghost last night.» What does gave up the ghost suggest? | It went on a trip | *It stopped working | It started singing | It was painted bright blue
test: «The old mining town is a ghost town now, with no people left.» What is a ghost town? | A town with lots of shops | A busy town by the sea | A town full of ghosts that scare people | *A town with almost no people left
test: The Chinese word «dǎnxiǎoguǐ» means what? | A ghost who sings in a cave | A brave hero | *A scaredy-cat | A kind of Chinese dinner
exam: In a game, a «ghost effect» makes a sprite faint or invisible. What does ghost mean in this sense? | *A very faint trace of something | A friendly robot | Pure gold | A loud noise
